comments.body:
[suggestion] I'd like to keep the existing form to benefit from type-safety:

```js
/** @type {import('stylelint').PublicApi['rules']} */
const rules = {
  // ...
};
```

So, what about the following way?

```js
/** @type {import('stylelint').PublicApi['rules']} */
const rules = {
	get 'alpha-value-notation'() {
		return getCachedRule('alpha-value-notation');
	},
  // ...
};
```

If doing so, we would have to use the `any` type to avoid a bunch of type errors like this:

```js
/**
 * NOTE: Use the `any` type to avoid a lot of useless casting.
 *
 * @typedef {any} Rule
 */

/** @type {Map<string, Promise<Rule>>} */

/**
 * @param {string} ruleName
 * @returns {Promise<Rule>}
 */
```

